Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:27.33,Kick,,0,0,0,,INDIA · EXPLAINED
Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:27.33,Title,,0,0,0,,TANKER HIT\NIN HORMUZ
Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:27.33,Foot,,0,0,0,,Source: Gulf News · News On AIR · Khaleej Times\NFull video on the channel
Dialogue: 1,0:00:00.15,0:00:02.40,Big,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1640)\fad(120,150)}24 INDIANS ABOARD
Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:08.38,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Twenty four Indian sailors were on a tanker hit in the Strait of Hormuz. Here is what we know.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.83,0:00:11.48,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}India's foreign ministry condemned the attack.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.48,0:00:16.04,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}It said attacks on commercial ships must end and free sailing must be restored.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.49,0:00:17.35,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Why it matters:
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.35,0:00:21.22,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}this is the second attack in a week on a tanker with Indian sailors.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.22,0:00:27.33,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}On the eleventh, another tanker was hit off the United Arab Emirates, and all twenty two crew were rescued.
